\section{Integral-State Regularization Analysis}
\label{sec:integral-regularization-theory}

The $\vct S=\vct 0$ pseudo-measurement is a deliberately nonphysical
regularizer: repeated updates suppress low-frequency integration drift but also
attenuate genuine low-frequency wave motion.  The reduced models below quantify
this drift--distortion tradeoff and separate the roles of covariance, Kalman
gain, and update cadence before adaptation is introduced.

